item","mr-3"],["src","/assets/images/annual-reports/download_24px.png","alt","",1,"d-inline",3,"click"],[1,"nav-link","d-none","d-md-inline",3,"click"],[1,"nav-item",3,"click"],["src","/assets/images/annual-reports/menu_24px.png","alt","",1,"d-inline"],[1,"nav-link","d-none","d-md-inline"],[1,"navbar-nav","ml-auto","pr-1","d-md-none"],["src","/assets/images/annual-reports/nav-close.png","alt","",1,"d-inline"],[1,"container-yellow-curve","curved"],[1,"container","container-head"],[1,"message-head"],[1,"message-left"],[1,"message-right"],["src","/assets/images/annual-reports/section-3-image-1.png"],["src","/assets/images/annual-reports/section-3-image-2.png"],[1,"container-message"],[1,"message"],[1,"message-author"],[1,"l-message"],[1,"r-message"],[3,"click"],["src","/assets/images/icon-expand_arrow.svg"],[1,"container-image-bottom"],[1,"image-bottom"],["src","/assets/images/shareholders-message/Change for Good.png"],[1,"d-none","shadow"],[1,"row"],[1,"col-4"],["href","#"],[1,"d-md-none"]],template:function(t,i){1&t&&(c(0,"div",0)(1,"nav",1)(2,"div",2)(3,"a",3),C(4,"img",4),u(),c(5,"button",5),C(6,"span",6),u(),c(7,"div",7)(8,"ul",8)(9,"li",9)(10,"img",10),D("click",function(r){return r.stopPropagation(),i.downloadPDF("https://www.cebupacificair.com/amplience-static/v1/static/2021-0512-CEB-AR2020-FA-Complete");}),u(),c(11,"a",11),D("click",function(r){return r.stopPropagation(),i.downloadPDF("https://www.cebupacificair.com/amplience-static/v1/static/2021-0512-CEB-AR2020-FA-Complete");}),p(12,"Download Report"),u()(),c(13,"li",12),D("click",function(){return i.toggleMenu();}),C(14,"img",13),c(15,"a",14),p(16,"Menu"),u()()(),c(17,"ul",15)(18,"li",12),D("click",function(){return i.toggleMenu();}),C(19,"img",16),u()()()()(),c(20,"main")(21,"div",17)(22,"div",2)(23,"div")(24,"h1"),p(25,"Message to Shareholders"),u()()()(),c(26,"section",18)(27,"div",19)(28,"div",20)(29,"h1")(30,"span"),p(31,"\u201c"),u(),p(32," The CEB family will continue to remain true to our commitment in providing safe, reliable and affordable services. Rest assured that soon enough, everyJuan will fly again. "),u()(),c(33,"div",21),C(34,"img",22)(35,"img",23),u()()(),c(36,"section",24)(37,"div",25)(38,"h1"),p(39,"To our dear Shareholders,"),u(),c(40,"h2"),p(41,"2020 WAS MOST CHALLENGING AS CEB FACES THE COVID CRISIS"),u(),c(42,"p"),p(43," 2020 was undeniably a very challenging year for Cebu Pacific and the entire aviation industry, as we were besieged by the great COVID-19 pandemic. Health and safety concerns brought down travel confidence and put up various travel restrictions, severely affecting CEB\u2019s operational and financial performance. "),u(),c(44,"p"),p(45," When an Enhanced Community Quarantine (ECQ) was first proclaimed middle of March 2020, CEB\u2019s commercial operations were grounded. We recommenced operations in June, albeit gradually, with most of the Philippines still on General Community Quarantine. Various documentary and regulatory travel requirements was also a significant challenge for CEB, other airlines and the travelling public. "),u(),c(46,"p"),p(47," From a total of 143,897 flights and 22.5 million passengers in 2019, flights in 2020 dropped 71% to only 41,804 and passenger count fell by 78% to just 5 million. Lower traffic amidst a domestic driven network during the restart period created a domino effect, resulting to a seat load factor of 76% despite 8% lower average fares. "),u(),c(48,"p"),p(49," These key statistics drove down CEB\u2019s revenues to Php22.6 billion, down 73% vs. 2019. We posted operating loss of P20.77 billion. These revenue levels are similar to levels 12 years back, and its the first time we\u2019ve posted an operating loss since we became a public company. Bottomline, we lost P22.2 billion, a major downturn vs. our Net Income of P9.13 billion posted in 2019. Liquidity was a key concern as we ended 2020 with a cash balance of P4.3B vs P18.2B end 2019. But with 74 aircraft, we ended 2020 with Total Assets of P128.5B, and a resilient net debt to equity of 3.17x. "),u(),c(50,"h2"),p(51,"CARGO SUPPLEMENTS PASSENGER OPERATIONS BETTER THAN EXPECTED"),u(),c(52,"p"),p(53," Passenger revenues were P12.6 billion, 80% lower, while ancillary revenues contributed Php4.6 billion. Cargo operations performed better than expected, supplementing passenger operations and surpassing ancillary revenues. It contributed P5.4B in revenues, 24% of total in 2020. Decline in cargo volumes were offset by an 81% increase in yield per kilo, driven by both cargo charter and freighter flights. "),u(),c(54,"p"),p(55," We ramped up cargo operations, and began operations of our 2nd ATR cargo freighter plane. We also started hybrid flights where one leg would carry pure cargo in both the belly and cabin, while the other leg carried passengers. This cross utilization allowed us to maximize fuel consumption and flight operations. We also configured one of our A330 aircraft for cargo operations, removing seats to allow cargo in the main cabin thus increasing our capacity for long haul cargo. "),u(),c(56,"h2"),p(57,"CEB RESPONDS WITH A FUTURE SIZE AND SHAPE STRATEGY"),u(),c(58,"p"),p(59," With the significant change in market conditions and industry dynamics, we saw the urgent need to implement a business transformation plan to ensure we survive and thrive post this pandemic crisis. CEB\u2019s future size and shape strategy involves right-sizing of our fleet, network and organization, to meet a reduced level of demand we now call the new normal. "),u(),c(60,"p"),p(61," We reshaped our fleet plan by optimizing our existing New Engine Option (NEO) as we are cognizant on the cost savings of its fuel efficiency. We also negotiated for deferral of our aircraft orders to later years, and opted to preserve unused aircraft in the less humid environment of Alice Springs, Australia. "),u(),c(62,"p"),p(63," This 2020, we also took full ownership of Aplus, our line maintenance provider, to optimize our maintenance program with better capacity planning in scale with CEB\u2019s network, and synergize functions using a common engineering and fleet maintenance platform. We also accelerated several process and policy enhancements, using various digital solutions to improve our operational efficiency. "),u(),c(64,"p"),p(65," We are conscious that this volatile Covid situation may continue to require us to cancel or adjust flights depending on capacity regulations. In order to give our passengers the most flexibility, we now provide several options for existing bookings. Passengers may rebook for travel within 90 days without any additional cost nor fare differentials. Passengers may also opt to refund, or alternatively, store the amount in a virtual CEB wallet valid for two years, and use this fund to either book a new flight or pay for add-ons such as baggage allowances, seat selection, and the like. More importantly, to better address the health and safety concerns, we have launched contactless flight and digital frontline procedures and improved self-service care channels, and on-the-spot, online flight disruption management. "),u(),c(66,"h2"),p(67,"FUNDRAISING PLAN POISED FOR LIMITED GROWTH AND BIG CHALLENGES"),u(),c(68,"p"),p(69," Underlying this whole transformation exercise is a highly conservative fundraising program that will provide sufficient liquidity in order to withstand the effects of the pandemic and allow us to thrive in the new normal. We developed our funding plan based on a stress case that conservatively projected a recovery beyond IATA\u2019s pronounced global recovery of aviation demand by 2024. This comprised 4 key initiatives. "),u(),c(70,"p"),p(71," I am very happy to note that we\u2019ve completed our key fundraising initiatives already. Last March 5, we signed a syndicated loan facility with various banks and financial institutions, providing us access to a committed term facility for as much as Php16 billion. "),u(),c(72,"p"),p(73," We have also successfully completed our convertible preferred shares (CPS) stock rights offering to existing shareholders. Our CPS were listed in the Philippine Stock Exchange on March 29,2021, and have provided CEB another Php12.5 billion. "),u(),c(74,"p"),p(75," Finally, last April 16, we signed an agreement for a US$250 Million convertible bond investment from Indigo Philippines LLC, an affiliate of Indigo Partners LLC, IFC or the International Finance Corporation, and IFC Emerging Asia Fund. We view Indigo, IFC and IFC Emerging Asia Fund not only as capital providers but also long-term partners in driving further improvements into the business as well as accelerating our sustainability agenda. "),u(),c(76,"p"),p(77," We have also restructured over US$150 Million in principal and lease payments, reducing cash outflow requirements in the near term, and are already engaged in ongoing discussions with lessors and creditors, for financing of our 2021 CAPEX requirements. "),u(),c(78,"h2"),p(79,"OUR HEARTFELT GRATITUDE FOR THE PAST 25 YEARS, AND BEYOND."),u(),c(80,"p"),p(81," I would like to express my appreciation and gratitude to our shareholders, board of directors, partners, employees, and our dear passengers, for your continued support and trust in CEB. The past 25 years has been quite a journey indeed! "),u(),c(82,"p"),p(83," I remain confident that CEB has the strength and resilience to grow amidst any further challenges ahead. The CEB family will continue to remain true to our commitment in providing safe, reliable and affordable services. Rest assured that soon enough, everyJuan will fly again. Maraming salamat po. "),u()(),c(84,"div",26)(85,"div",27)(86,"h5"),p(87,"Lance Y. Gokongwei"),u(),c(88,"p"),p(89,"President and CEO"),u()(),c(90,"div",28)(91,"a",29),D("click",function(){return i.scrollToTop();}),p(92,"Back To top "),C(93,"img",30),u()()()(),c(94,"section",31)(95,"div",32),C(96,"img",33),u()()(),c(97,"aside",34)(98,"div",2)(99,"div",35)(100,"div",36)(101,"ul")(102,"li")(103,"a"