must visit in the city include the Dominican-founded Saint Peter Metropolitan Cathedral and the Buntun Bridge \u2013 a steel truss bridge known to be the longest river bridge in the country and extends 1.37km over the Cagayan River. "),u(),c(75,"p"),p(76," Just outside the city, you can also visit the Calvary Hills, a popular Holy Week spot; Pe\xf1ablanca, a place popular to spelunkers; the 19th century church Basilica Minore of Our Lady of Piat, where one can have a tase of steamed buns called pawa; and the town of Santa Ana, known for its white-sand beach and the shooting location of "),c(77,"em"),p(78,"Survivor USA."),u()(),c(79,"p")(80,"strong"),p(81,"HIGHLIGHTS"),u()(),c(82,"ul")(83,"li"),p(84," Get around town on the humble tricycle (or \u201ctricy\u201d to locals) or the horse-drawn karitela, the most common modes of public transport. "),u(),c(85,"li"),p(86," Make your way to Iguig where you'll find the Calvary Hills\u2019 life-sized statues depicting the 14 Stations of the Cross. "),u(),c(87,"li"),p(88," For a hefty dose of sun, sand and sea, make your way up north to the coastal town of Santa Ana, which holds bragging rights for being a Survivor USA shooting location. "),u()(),c(89,"p")(90,"strong"),p(91,"AIRPORTS"),u()(),c(92,"ul")(93,"li"),p(94,"Cebu Pacific has several flights to Tuguegarao\u2019s Tuguegarao Airport"),u()(),c(95,"p")(96,"strong"),p(97,"WHEN TO VISIT"),u()(),c(98,"p"),p(99," The best time to get on flights to Tuguegarao is in the second week of August, so you'll catch the Pavvurulun Afi Festival, the grandest of the fiestas in the Cagayan Valley. Known as Cagayan\u2019s fire festival, it\u2019s the celebration of Tuguegarao City\u2019s patron, Saint Hyacinth of Poland, and features a parade of torch-bearing dancers, along with cultural activities and a trade fair. "),u(),c(100,"p")(101,"strong"),p(102,"Book flights to Tuguegarao"),u()(),c(103,"p"),p(104," The largest airline in the Philippines, Cebu Pacific has multiple flights to Tuguega